    <h2 id="collection-and-library">The collection and the Library</h2>

    <p>
      <strong>The creator keeps his rights.</strong> Publishing here transfers
      nothing. The originals stay where he put them: all fifteen Soap Creek
      monographs, the 1999 thesis and the 1989 Auto Tour are on his own site as
      PDFs, and the Elliott interviews are on ORWW. The Library's pages are a
      page-by-page mirror of what he already publishes, plus the indexes,
      places, people and timeline the Library built on top of it.
    </p>

    <p>
      <strong>The Library publishes with his participation.</strong> He
      reviewed this edition with the Library in August 2026; his written
      permission for it is being recorded and the formal instrument follows.
      He gives up nothing by allowing it, and he can ask for any part of it to
      come down.
    </p>

    <p>
      The monographs were printed and funded by the OSU Research Forests and
      the College of Forestry, and the narrators' consents ran to institutions
      rather than to him personally. Those interests are set out item by item
      on the <a href="/collections/zybach/provenance/">provenance page</a>;
      reuse is covered under <a href="/collections/zybach/how-to-cite/#rights">how
      to cite</a>.
    </p>

